---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
---

<Base
  title="About the Publication Data"
  description="How the SES publications database is collected, curated, and kept current: weekly Google Scholar updates, automated matching, and human verification."
>
  <PageHero
    title="About the Publication Data"
    lede="How we collect, curate, and publish the research record of the School of Earth and Sustainability."
  />
  <div class="prose-ses mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10">
    <p>
      The <a href="/publications/">publications explorer</a> and
      <a href="/research/">research-impact dashboard</a> on this site are built from a curated
      database of peer-reviewed publications by SES faculty and students.
    </p>

    <h2>How the data is collected</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Scholar, weekly.</strong> Every week, an automated pipeline checks the
        Google Scholar profile of each SES faculty member, refreshes citation counts for every
        publication, and adds newly published papers.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Since 2009.</strong> Statistics cover publications from 2009 onward, the era of
        the modern school.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Peer-reviewed only.</strong> Conference abstracts, preprints, and similar
        materials are filtered out automatically.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How authors are identified</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Faculty matching.</strong> Publications are attributed to SES faculty by matching
        author names (including initials and name variants) against the faculty roster, bounded by
        each person's years at NAU.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Student identification.</strong> Graduate-student co-authors are detected against
        the SES student roster, with publication dates checked against enrollment periods.
        Undergraduate co-authors are added by hand.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Human verification.</strong> Records are reviewed and corrected by people;
        verified records are protected from automated changes (except citation counts).
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What the numbers mean</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>H-index</strong> is computed school-wide: the largest number <em>h</em> such that
        <em>h</em> SES publications have each been cited at least <em>h</em> times.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Citations</strong> come from Google Scholar and change continuously; our copies
        refresh weekly.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Student papers</strong> count publications with at least one SES graduate or
        undergraduate student among the authors.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Infrastructure</h2>
    <p>
      The site is a static Astro build hosted on GitHub Pages. The publication database lives as
      version-controlled CSV files in the site's repository; every change is tracked, validated,
      and reviewable. Weekly data updates and the monthly student-research news features are
      handled by automated agents supervised by SES faculty.
    </p>
    <p>
      Spotted an error in a record?
      <a href="/contact/">Let us know</a> and we'll fix it.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
